  <NAME>Homo sapiens</NAME>
  <TITLE>Mitochondrial carrier homolog 2 (MTCH2) regulates the differentiation of AML cells by controlling pyruvate entry into the mitochondria, nuclear localization of pyruvate dehydrogenase complex and H3 and H4 histone acetylation</TITLE>
  <DESCRIPTION>Inhibiting MTCH2 or the Mitochondrial Pyruvate Carrier increased levels of pyruvate and pyruvate dehydrogenase in the nucleus leading to differentiation and loss of stemness in AML. Overall design: Gene expression analysis upon knock-down of MTCH2 by two independent shRNAs</DESCRIPTION>
